    },
    "On a lens that can't save RAW, the phone's camera processes the photo. nope. marks the camera \"Processed\" before you take it, unless you turn off Processed Marker in Settings, and the photo's details always say so. Tap the marker to see what processing that lens's photos get." : {
      "comment" : "Issue #80; docs/PRIVACY.md, \"Processing\". \"Processed\" is the marker's first word and Processed Marker the name of nope.'s own switch; use their translations. RAW is a file format name. Keep \"nope.\" unchanged. Must not claim more than the English. Honesty wording: a fluent human must review every translation before release.",
